b 137535134332: 20807 passed, 892 skipped, 0 failed, 0 errors (finished 2026-11-23 00:25 PST). tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py (12 cases) and tests/unit/test_rev_path_read_guard.py carry no Windows skip and are selected by the sweep (they failed by name in red run 45069422395), so they passed on main. AC1/AC2: the guard passes on main (all 16 reads use cat-file blob). All acceptance criteria met.","timestamp":1795422390854321001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1795261581107500001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b6b636ca-e8a3-4dad-b9bf-a0cfe4119cb5","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"a2da-e61b-989e-4862"},{"link_uuid":"09eecded-c4f6-4f95-a2cd-421ce62d8474","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9f5a-38c7-de9c-4e56"}],"description":"## Observation\nOn Windows, `git show <rev>:<path>` run without `--` dies with exit 128 and `fatal: failed to stat '<rev>:<path>': Filename too long` when cwd plus the argument reaches MAX_PATH. Measured in `sweep (windows)` run 44899637411 (2026-11-21 PST) for `fsck_restore`; a shorter temp path passed (run 44899366277), and `git cat-file blob` passed (run 44900309390). cold-censorable-armedcrab fixed `fsck_restore` (4f14a00093f, Gerrit 3511). This ticket covers the rest.\n\n## Sites on origin/main 39d78c81fd5 (`git show <rev>:<path>`, no `--`)\nProduct, 12 reads:\n- src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py:98, :122, :164 (`tickets:.gitattributes`, `tickets:.gitignore`, `tickets:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_commands/init.py:440 (`tickets:.pre-commit-config.yaml`)\n- src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py:108 (`<rev>:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:151 (`<tickets ref>:<path>`)\n- src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:195 (`<spec>` = `<ref>:<prefix>rebar.toml`/`pyproject.toml`)\n- src/rebar/_store/compat.py:180, :274, :296 (`<ref or commit>:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py:67 (`tickets:<projects.json>`)\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py:217 (`HEAD:<path>`)\n\nScripts, 4 reads: scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:517 (run by `make lint`), scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py:53, :56, scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py:43.\n\nSeveral sites treat a non-zero exit as \"absent\", so a deep Windows path misreads an existing object as missing (the `_init_ensures` units then re-create and commit a file that exists). Others (`bridge_fsck`, `_opcert_gate_config`, `check_complexity_baseline`) fail closed on a healthy store.\n\n## Root cause\nFor revision-parsing verbs (`show`, `log`, `diff`, `rev-list`) git runs a filename-ambiguity check on every revision argument unless `--` ends the revisions. That check stats `<cwd>\\<rev>:<path>`; on Windows the stat fails with ENAMETOOLONG at MAX_PATH and git aborts. `git cat-file blob <rev>:<path>` resolves the object name only and never stats it (run 44900309390). `rev-parse` and `cat-file -e` on a valid name skip the stat too, so their uses are out of class.\n\n## Approach\n1. Replace each of the 16 reads with `git cat-file blob <rev>:<path>` through the same wrapper, keeping each site's `check`/`text`/timeout/returncode handling. `cat-file blob` prints the same bytes as `git show` on a blob (neither runs textconv) and exits non-zero for a missing path or ref, so every \"absent\" branch keeps its meaning. Update comments, docstrings and the `bridge_fsck` `operation=` label that name `show`. No config key, env var or flag.\n2. Guard: new `tests/unit/test_rev_path_read_guard.py` AST-scans `src/rebar/**/*.py` and `scripts/**/*.py`. A git call (callee name containing `git`, or argv list literal starting `\"git\"`) is reported when (a) its verb is `show`/`log`/`diff`/`rev-list`, it has no `--`, and an argument is a `<rev>:<path>` literal, f-string or same-function local bound to one; or (b) its verb is `show` with no `--` and no commit-display flag (`-s`, `--no-patch`, `--stat`, `--name-only`, `--name-status`, `--format…`, `--pretty…`), which catches a path that arrives as a parameter. The message names file:line and the remedy. Synthetic positive and negative cases pin the detector (f-string, literal, local, parameter, `-s --format` read, `cat-file blob`, `rev-parse`, trailing `--`, `add_parser(\"show\")`).\n3. Behaviour: new `tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py` commits every file the product sites read on a `tickets` branch, adds a `--no-checkout` linked worktree (the shape of `.tickets-tracker`) padded so `len(cwd) + 1 + len(argument) >= 260` while its `.git` file stays under MAX_PATH, and drives each product read through its real function: the 4 ensure units return `ok`, `_commit_precommit` makes no commit, `_record_at`, `_unknown_event_types_from_ref`, `_committed_toml`, the 3 compat readers and `_fixture_files` return the committed content. It runs on every platform; on Windows it reproduces the MAX_PATH condition. A temp dir too long to build the case fails the test with that diagnostic rather than skipping.\n4. `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py::test_scan_failures_raise_public_rebar_error` keys its fake on `args[0] == \"show\"`; change it to `cat-file`.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py, src/rebar/_commands/init.py, src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py, src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py, src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py, src/rebar/_store/compat.py, src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py, src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py, scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py, scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py, scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py, tests/unit/test_rev_path_read_guard.py (new), tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py (new), tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py. No `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/*.args` line belongs to this bug.\n\n## Testing\n- Guard red/green: run it on origin/main (fails, 16 sites) and on the fix (passes).\n- Windows, pre-merge: push the fixed tree to `tmp/b5-comic-heavyset-jerboa` and dispatch `test.yml`; push the same tree with only the product and script edits reverted to `tmp/b5-comic-heavyset-jerboa-red` and dispatch. Record both `sweep (windows)` run ids. Delete both branches.\n- Windows, post-merge: the first scheduled `test.yml` run on main containing the merge commit.\n- `make verify` through verify-slot.sh before the push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] All 16 reads listed above (12 product, 4 script) use `git cat-file blob`.\n- [x] No `git show`/`log`/`diff`/`rev-list` call in `src/rebar` or `scripts` passes a `<rev>:<path>` argument without `--` (the guard test passes on the fix).\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_rev_path_read_guard.py` fails on origin/main 39d78c81fd5 (outcome in a comment).\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py` fails in the pre-merge `sweep (windows)` run without the product change (run id in a comment).\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py` passes in the pre-merge `sweep (windows)` run with the product change (run id in a comment).\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py` passes in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the merge (run id in a comment).\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0 on the pushed tree (log path in a comment).\n- [x] The change is merged to main at LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 (Gerrit number, merge SHA in a comment).","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/init.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/compat.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_rev_path_read_guard.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"},{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py","reason":"comic-heavyset-jerboa: read <rev>:<path> with cat-file blob, not git show (Windows MAX_PATH stat)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9f5a-38c7-de9c-4e56"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"0e080833-2d99-4158-bd32-b143faaf37f6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticke